WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
Water keeps you alive.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.740
A diamond is just pretty to look at.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.340
Yet the diamond costs far more.

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.590
Pay can look just as strange.

5
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.340
Some of the most useful
jobs pay less than jobs

6
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.440
that seem far less useful.

7
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.720
So what really decides
how much a job pays?

8
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.840
In this mission, you'll build
the diagram economists use

9
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.280
for any job market, one curve at a time.

10
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.360
Then you'll shift demand
for workers in a graph lab,

11
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.100
predict what happens to pay,

12
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.290
and test it.

13
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.650
Your mission: find out
what really sets a wage.
